{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521160-nitpick-regarding-vampiric-powers","id":1521160,"title":"Nitpick regarding Vampiric powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-21T19:44:52-07:00","id":1521160,"title":"Nitpick regarding Vampiric powers","content":"When I first delved into VTM, I immersed myself in the lore and read a lot about the incredible powers that vampires wield against mortals and each other, how Disciplines used by established clans and the Blood Magic of the Tremere played a crucial role in the Camarilla's survival, and how Sabbat vampires harnessed their powers in terrifying ways which put the Camarilla on edge.<br /> <br /> However, when I actually looked at the specific powers available to vampires, did questions start popping up. Why don't vampires with Dominate 5 use it to carry out their tasks during daylight hours? Can a vampire utilize Animalism 5 to avoid becoming Wight? Why don't the Giovanni use Auspex 5 to journey to the underworld instead of investing time and effort into the Ash Path?Why don't younger Kolduns incorporate city spirits into their magic? If there are Krainas associated with demons and Enoch, surely there could be one tied to the city itself? <br /> <br /> Powers like Spirit Manipulation, Elemental Mastery, Green Path, Weather Manipulation, and the Evil Eye are intriguing because they grant vampires control over beings and aspects of society that humanity has depended on since ancient times\u2014spirits, agriculture, and weather. Yet you dont really hear vampires in lore using these powers that often. Of course, there are also paths such as Path of Ushabti, Divine Hand, Flow of Ashe, and Orisha's Fortune which should have some overarching effect on vampire society, yet for all intents and purposes, they might as well not exist.<br /> <br /> Of course I'm not saying that the powers here are easy to learn, I just feel that they are relatively easier to learn than others depending on your Clan/Bloodline/Generation.\u200b<br /> <br /> Anyway, thats the end of my nitpick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.nodiatis.com/pub/18.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27313-hello","name":"Hello","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T01:19:51-07:00","id":1521165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521160-nitpick-regarding-vampiric-powers#post1521160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't vampires with Dominate 5 use it to carry out their tasks during daylight hours?</div> </div> </div> </div>First, while using posession, your body lies in a torpid state, defenseless against any actions made toward it. <br /> The posessed is is aware of events only in a distorted, dreamlike fashion<br /> But these are &quot;minor&quot; porblems, the mayor one is: while the vampire may also venture out during the day in the mortal form, her own body must be awake to do so, requiring a successful roll to remain awake <br /> This is something a very few vampire is able to do<br /> As a side note, any damage the victim\u2019s body sustains is also applied to the character\u2019s body (though the Kindred may soak as normal) is also problematic<br /> But the main reason is the staying awake during day part and the fact not many vampire know Dominate 5 and the ones that do, are old/smart enough to use it only when there is no other choice - a well conditioned ghoul perhaps is more than enough<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521160-nitpick-regarding-vampiric-powers#post1521160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a vampire utilize Animalism 5 to avoid becoming Wight?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> No<br /> I mean you have to use that discipline to unleash your Beast onto others<br /> Actually it potentially could even worsen your situation, because of defeneration; morally it is not that good to &quot;curse&quot; someone with your own Beast and a very few Path or Road looks favorably to such action, Humanity? No, really no.<br /> Not to mention the inherent danger of losing your Beast and have to track it down and lure back to you - or kill the vessel in question, and that again not really good to your mental health<br /> And if you are low enough to not to care about such things?<br /> You are not really have any reason to NOT to embrace your Beast and its urges - from RP perspective <br /> If you become older, you will have Conquer the Beast anyway, both to control her frenzies and to enter them at will<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521160-nitpick-regarding-vampiric-powers#post1521160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't the Giovanni use Auspex 5 to journey to the underworld instead of investing time and effort into the Ash Path?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Because with Auspex 5 you don't journey to the underworld, but the sending their consciousness into the High Umbra not the Middle Umbra nor the Low/Dark Umbra <br /> It is called astral form for a reason, not ghostly form <br /> Storytellers are encouraged to make trips into the spirit world as bizarre, mysterious, and dreamlike as possible. The world beyond is a vivid and fantastic place, where the true nature of things is stronger and often strikingly different from their earthly appearances.<br /> this is actually the accurate descritpion of Astral Penumbra and a bit of the Vulgate (the Realm of base thought, which features much of the concepts present in the material world. The geography of the Vulgate organizes itself in domains of cultural influence arranged in historic progression - the cities of the United States would be depicted as one super-megatropolis with every significant landmark arranged.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521160-nitpick-regarding-vampiric-powers#post1521160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't younger Kolduns incorporate city spirits into their magic? If there are Krainas associated with demons and Enoch, surely there could be one tied to the city itself?</div> </div> </div> </div>Long since the days passed of the ancient Kolduns who were inventors<br /> But still, some remained<br /> The Bia\u0142owieza Kraina done similar with the whole of the Bia\u0142owieza Forest (a forest on the border between Belarus and Poland. It is one of the last and largest remaining parts of the immense primeval forest that once stretched across the European Plain.) invented by Djabelek, Master of Bia\u0142owieza Forest a 6th Generation Koldun<br /> But the main reason... Koldunism is not a &quot;city&quot; magic<br /> It is Nature magic, using the spirits of nature and elements (and in a few times, Banes)<br /> The City especially a large one that would have a Spirit, a City Parent (more commonly known as a City Father or City Mother) a spirit that embodies a particular city is not that attractive to the Koldun<br /> But if you ment spirits found in a City... well they are not really nature or elemental spirits, sure Smog and such could be found there, but the Koldun are very protective of their land and they have a nice tradition to hunt &quot;Kupalas&quot; - banes that taint and torture their lands, puting any Garou to shame<br /> Still, in theory it would be possible if a young Koldun would have time and resources to invent such things - but the Kolduns are not really social cretures and hoard their secrets jelously<br /> Basically the only reason they not conquered the world yet, becasue two Koldun would refuse to work together or share their secrets<br /> But if a youngster would invent such a &quot;heretical path&quot;, they probably would react how the Tremere reacted to the Technomancy\u200b... with disgust and fear just without the rigid structure of the Tremere and would try to purge such diabolical knowledge<br /> Maybe the future of Koldunism lies with those inventors, but so far no one stepped forward... or survived to present such a path<br /> Storyteller descretion? I would allow the invention of such Path, but would be... consequences and the least would be the Glass Walkers<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hello</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521160-nitpick-regarding-vampiric-powers#post1521160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Powers like Spirit Manipulation, Elemental Mastery, Green Path, Weather Manipulation, and the Evil Eye are intriguing because they grant vampires control over beings and aspects of society that humanity has depended on since ancient times\u2014spirits, agriculture, and weather. Yet you dont really hear vampires in lore using these powers that often. Of course, there are also paths such as Path of Ushabti, Divine Hand, Flow of Ashe, and Orisha's Fortune which should have some overarching effect on vampire society, yet for all intents and purposes, they might as well not exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Becasue they are very specialized and known only by a few, but there are lore for ecample, about the ancient weather controlling vampires of old who were gods, especially in Summer and Egypt<br /> The Setite Akhu or Dur-an-Ki is respected and feard for a reason","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T01:39:48-07:00","id":1521168,"title":"","content":"The most common or often discussed Discipline Powers - together with cooperation, teamwork, honest effort, and reliable planning - are often more than enough to carry out objectives, achieve satisfactory results, and progress with ambitions and goals. In some books the most reliable and popular Powers receive additional boosts or options - for example it is mentioned in Revised Venture Clanbook that there is an option to choose to lower the number of successes of a Presence result by one, if a Vampire prefers a less potent outcome.<br /> <br /> Thus the more specialized or powerful Powers are often not needed. That does not mean that they are not used. Many Kindred are honest and regular Discipline users and experts, with all the variety, vision, creativity, and innovation that would be noted and expected.<br /> <br /> As to why some mystical or normal concepts, results, areas, and ideas are not more often discussed and described ; and why they are not within the meaning and results of the most common or popular Abilities and Powers of Vampires. This is to a considerable and significant extent the case because the game and the setting descriptions are focused and tilted towards relatively young and ambitious Camarilla Vampires or Anarch Vampires. Political, economic, and social interactions and challanges are most commonly brought up and described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T09:10:19-07:00","id":1521195,"title":"","content":"I never looked to deeply into that myself, but as a general rule is that using the advanced levels of the Disciplines comes with all sorts of drawbacks such as placing your mind into a mortal so you can do some daytime actions leaves your body in a dangerous state that rivals could use to get rid of you or move into jail and not to mention the toll it might take on your servant. Also using the disciplines uses up energy and the more powerful uses would definetly speed that up and you need to feed more to keep yourself sane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-22-2023, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T10:23:12-07:00","id":1521200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> 