rs/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-22T10:40:49-07:00","id":1521204,"title":"","content":"Well to be fair, in Mage, there is technically no cannon and set cosmology, as the whole point of Mage is that the universe is very subjective, and the books keep contradicting themselves... but someone who is more familiar with Mage than me correct me please if I'm wrong<br /> Beyond the Barriers: The Book of Worlds describes some umbra realms and how some of them can be entered from even Earth, thats true and of course both in Werewolf and Kindred of the East there are ways to enter to one Realm from another travel deep and far and have all sorts of dangerous andventures<br /> (And if we are not careful, we might end up Vicissitude is dragged back from the Deep Umbra by a 4th Generation Tzimsice named Andeleon, who ate from <i>something</i> there from what he wasn't suposed to... )<br /> Keep in mind, even if it would be possible to travel to the Dark Umbra/Underworld with Auspex 5 your astral projection is linked to your body with a silver cord - and if its snaps, you are basically toast, so wandering to far or too deep is not the brightest of ideas anyway<br /> May God have mercy on your toon's soul of your Storyteller is even a bit familiar with other settings and in a bad mood... trust me, it is bad enough what you could potentially find in the Astral without giving your ST ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-23T09:56:40-07:00","id":1521259,"title":"","content":"This also reminds me of the debates on why certain superheroes or villians didn't use there most powerful attacks constantly and overlooking the fact it might take time to generate the energy to unleash it and may take a physical or mental toll on the person and it would be considered an act of last resort when all else fails.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}